-- title:
--   Strong approximation for norm-one quaternions away from a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ with $a<0$ and $b<0$, so that $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is definite, and let $O\subseteq\mathbb H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in O$, $O$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb Q$-span is all of $\mathbb H$, and it is finitely generated. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ at which $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ contains a nonzero non-unit (the splitting hypothesis `hv`). Let $y$ be a unit of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^f$, $\mathbb A^f$ the finite adele ring of $\mathbb Q$, such that for every prime $w\neq v$ and every ring isomorphism $\varphi:\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\to\mathbb H[\mathbb Q_w,a,b]$ satisfying $\varphi(z\otimes r)=r\cdot z$ coordinatewise on the four coordinates of $z$, the reduced norm $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-a\,x_{\mathrm{imI}}^2-b\,x_{\mathrm{imJ}}^2+ab\,x_{\mathrm{imK}}^2$ of $\varphi(y_w)$ equals $1$, where $y_w$ is the image of $y$ under evaluation at $w$. Then there are a unit $\beta$ of $\mathbb H$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^f$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\beta)=1$, with $u$ in the stabiliser of the adelic box of $O$ (the additive subgroup generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in O$ and $\alpha$ integral at every place), with $g_w=1$ for all $w\neq v$, and with $y=\iota(\beta)\,g\,u$, where $\iota$ is the diagonal embedding of $\mathbb H^\times$ induced by $z\mapsto z\otimes 1$.
--
--   This is strong approximation for the norm-one group of a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$ relative to a finite place where the algebra splits, stated as a double-coset decomposition $y\in\mathbb H^1\cdot\mathbb H_v^\times\cdot\widehat O^\times$ in which the global factor is pinned to have reduced norm exactly $1$ rather than merely being invertible. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, for instance in the construction of units of prescribed reduced norm acting on the coset graph attached to $O$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_nrd_eq_one_and_eq_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_mul_of_forall_nrd_eq_one.lean

